A romantic weekend near Amboise comes down to very little: a room with real character, a dinner you do not have to drive out to find, and enough to fill two days without ever rushing. At the Château de la Huberdière, in Nazelles-Négron, we welcome couples who come for exactly that.

Here is how we suggest shaping those two days together, hour by hour, with the stops worth the detour and the ones you can skip.

## Where should you go for a romantic weekend near Amboise?

The Loire Valley remains the safest bet for a romantic weekend in France, and the Amboise area is its geographical heart. The royal château, the Clos Lucé, Chenonceau and Chaumont-sur-Loire all sit within thirty minutes, without ever rejoining the motorway.

La Huberdière stands at Nazelles-Négron, directly opposite Amboise on the other bank of the Loire. You are 2 hrs 20 from Paris by car and 30 minutes from the Saint-Pierre-des-Corps TGV station. The estate is a sixteenth-century family home: 10 rooms, 14 hectares of walled grounds, and a silence that begins at the gate. Room details and availability are on the [stay at the château](/en/boutique-hotel-amboise) page.

Our advice for a weekend away as a couple: one base, and you travel out from it. Changing hotel every night spoils half the pleasure, and the other half goes into the suitcases.

## Day 1: arrive early and plan nothing

The best decision of a weekend for two is to arrive late on Friday afternoon and plan nothing before dinner. It is the one moment of the stay when you can genuinely slow down, and it is the one most couples give up.

![Period bathroom with a claw-foot bath and blue-bordered tiling](/images/inline/chambres/chambre-18.webp "Several rooms have kept their original claw-foot baths. Those are the first to go.")

You drop the bags, push the shutters open, and the park does the rest. From April to October the heated pool is in service: you swim as the light drops over the Vouvray slopes, with nobody around. The rest of the year there is a fire in the drawing room and two armchairs waiting for precisely this.

If you are coming from Paris by train, plan on a car from Saint-Pierre-des-Corps. The estate is in the countryside, which is the whole point, but the châteaux cannot be reached on foot.

## Dinner in the evening, without getting back in the car

The real luxury of a romantic weekend at a château is dining on site and going up to bed ten metres later. Every evening except Sunday, we serve generous sharing boards made from market and kitchen garden produce.

![Table laid in the panelled dining room, door open onto the grounds](/images/inline/restauration/restauration-02.webp "Eating in saves the twenty-minute drive back, which is the whole point of a table d'hôtes.")

I am Italian, and on Thursday evenings dinner is entirely Italian, fresh pasta included. It is the meal that comes up most often in what our guests tell us afterwards, and that is no accident: we cook here the way you cook at home, not the way a hotel restaurant does. Evening service is reserved for residents, outside private events. The days and the formats are set out on the [dining](/en/chateau-dining-touraine) page.

A couple who dine at the estate gain two hours on a couple who drive back into town looking for a table, look for another because the first is full, and then drive home. Those two hours are the weekend.

## Day 2: the Loire châteaux, just the two of you

Two châteaux in one day, not three: that is the rule that separates a break from a route march. Beyond that, you visit with one eye on your watch and come home more tired than you left.

Our markers from the estate, for a successful weekend in a Loire château:

- the royal château of Amboise and the Clos Lucé, Leonardo da Vinci's last home, ten minutes away
- Chenonceau, set across the Cher, twenty minutes away, the most photogenic of the two banks
- Chaumont-sur-Loire and its international garden festival, twenty-five minutes away, April to November
- Villandry and its formal gardens, forty minutes away, for anyone wanting to push further

If you were to keep only one for a first weekend together, take Chenonceau in the morning at opening, before the coaches. The gallery over the Cher at half past nine, without the crowd, bears no resemblance to the same gallery at three in the afternoon. Our guide to [visiting the Loire châteaux](/en/blog/visiting-loire-chateaux) gives the opening times, the distances and the running order that avoids the queues.

## The Vouvray vineyards, the stop couples forget

The Vouvray vineyard starts literally at the end of the park, and it is the most underrated stop of a romantic weekend in Touraine. The cellars are cut into the tuffeau stone, tastings happen without ceremony, and the winemakers take their time.

Vouvray and Montlouis-sur-Loire fill half a day, slotted between two château visits. You will find dry chenins and sparkling wines that hold their own against many champagnes, at prices that bear no comparison. Count on one cellar, two at most: nobody remembers the third.

## Which room should you choose for a weekend for two?

Our rooms do not all serve the same purpose, and for a weekend away as a couple, two or three stand out. Each of our 10 rooms carries its own name and a decor that belongs to it alone: Paradis Sauvage, Bouquet, Giboulée, Pêche, Bleu Indien.

No two are alike, and that is deliberate. For a couple, we tend to steer you towards the rooms facing the park, with the original ceiling heights and a proper window onto the century-old trees. Tell us the stay is a break for two when you enquire and we will advise on the room. To understand what sets a lived-in house apart from somewhere you simply pass through, our article on [bed and breakfasts in Amboise](/en/blog/bed-and-breakfast-amboise) sets out what people are really after in a place with character.

## What budget for a romantic weekend at a château?

For two people, a romantic weekend at a charming château usually falls between 150 and 300 euros a night, homemade breakfast included. The price depends on the room, the season and the length of the stay.

To that, add dinner on site and monument entries, around twenty euros per person per château. A full weekend for two, two nights, two dinners and three visits, stays well below the cost of the same escape in a city-centre hotel, where a restaurant table has to be added every evening. We show real availability rather than a single headline rate, on the [stay](/en/boutique-hotel-amboise) page.

## Which season should you choose for a break for two?

September and October are the two best months for a romantic weekend in the Loire Valley, and nobody says it often enough. The vines turn red, the pool stays warm until the end of September, and you can cross the walkways of Chenonceau without using your elbows.

![Pink and fuchsia peonies in bloom in the château garden](/images/inline/jardin-fleurs/jardin-fleurs-04.webp "The peonies flower in late May. It is the most requested fortnight of the year.")

Spring has the gardens of Villandry and Chaumont in a soft light. Winter has absolute quiet, a fire in the drawing room and gentler rates: it is also the season when couples come to look the place over for something bigger, and we describe that in our article on [winter weddings at the château](/en/blog/winter-wedding-chateau-loire). Summer is still beautiful, but it is the only time you share the valley with everyone else.

